  "report": "Implementation review passed; operator acceptance remains separate.\n\nRESULT: accepted\n\n**OBSERVED:** All 69 uncommitted paths match checkpoint `2653c43a…` by file hash; only `rust/crates/rgr/src/presentation/test_status.rs` changed since review-1. Its `checked_add` now rejects the overflowing count, and the test covers `u64::MAX`. The renamed producer test serializes the actual agent DTO. Review-1 F-1 is closed; no new finding or decision is required.\n\n**Slice-scoped obligations:** RG-REQ-001-L01–L10, RG-REQ-002-L01–L11, RG-REQ-011-L01–L10, and P-TESA-01–04 are accepted on the retained review evidence plus this correction. RG-REQ-011-L11 is withdrawn; this review makes no latency claim. The 68 byte-identical paths retain their individual review-1 assessments; the revised `test_status.rs` is accepted.\n\n**Verification:** TESA-C01–C06 rely on the earlier builder-executed checks; their code did not change. TESA-C07–C12 and C11 rely on revision-2 **BUILDER-EXECUTED** logs, not an independent Cargo or isolated-`rmap` run. **OBSERVED:** `/tmp/tesa-c07.txt` reports 1,349 passing tests, including the malformed-block and producer-serialization tests. The C09/C10 logs report, respectively, an identical leveldb store and 788 Poco `testsuite/` files changing to test status. Prior source inspection confirmed Poco `ArrayTest.cpp:19` (`ArrayTest::ArrayTest(…)`) as a primary witness and leveldb `util/testutil.h:9` (`#include \"gtest/gtest.h\"`) as a marker-classified residual.\n\nUnder the hood, the shared pure path rule derives uncertainty from a tracked path and its stored test flag; the renderer now refuses internally inconsistent counts rather than presenting them as measured facts. That preserves the VISION’s distinction between extracted facts and what an agent must investigate. Acceptance is of this implementation slice, not a claim that the parent requirements are globally complete."
